meta {
  name: create package
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/packages/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required. English title.
    "title_en": "20-Class Package",

    // Optional Spanish title. Falls back to the English one when blank.
    "title_es": "Paquete de 20 Clases",

    // Optional. Shown on the pricing card.
    "description_en": "20 x 60-minute private lessons. Best value. Valid for 6 months.",
    "description_es": "",

    // Optional. URL from POST /administrator/upload/.
    "image_url": "",

    // Optional, defaults to 1. How many classes the purchase grants.
    "total_classes": 20,

    // Optional, defaults to 90. Days from purchase until the package expires.
    // Spec: 90 for the 10-class, 180 for the 20-class.
    "validity_days": 180,

    // Required. USD, two decimal places.
    // NOTE: the 20-class price is still unresolved -- the spec says $250.00 and
    // the copy deck says $254.64. Confirm with Rosa/Mateo before launch.
    "price": "250.00",

    // Optional, defaults to false. Marks the discounted Assessment & First
    // Lesson: it becomes the highlighted card and can only be bought once per
    // email. Only one package should carry this flag.
    "is_first_lesson": false,

    // Optional, defaults to 0. Ascending display order on the pricing section.
    "sort_order": 3,

    // Optional, defaults to true. False hides it from the public API.
    "active": true,

    // Optional list of teacher UUIDs this package may be booked with.
    // An EMPTY list (the default) means unrestricted -- every active teacher
    // is offered, which is what all four seeded packages do. Send ids here to
    // limit the package, e.g. senior teachers only on the 20-class pack.
    "teachers": []
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  `GET` lists every package including inactive ones (the public endpoint hides
  inactive), `POST` creates one. `GET`/`PUT`/`PATCH`/`DELETE
  /administrator/packages/<id>/` handle a single package. Not paginated.

  `DELETE` deactivates rather than deletes -- purchases reference packages with
  `PROTECT`, and a deleted package would orphan someone's invoice history.

  `teachers` drives `GET /public/packages/<id>/teachers/` (booking step 2) and is
  enforced again at checkout and on portal bookings. Empty means unrestricted,
  not "no teachers". The read-only `teacher_names` echoes the assignment back.

  Editing a package never rewrites existing purchases: each `StudentPackage`
  keeps a frozen `package_data` snapshot from the moment of sale.

  ## API example response
  {
    "id": "6936886f-cd74-4edf-9099-0097b1a2c3d4",
    "title_en": "20-Class Package",
    "title_es": "Paquete de 20 Clases",
    "description_en": "20 x 60-minute private lessons. Best value. Valid for 6 months.",
    "description_es": "",
    "image_url": "",
    "total_classes": 20,
    "validity_days": 180,
    "price": "250.00",
    "is_first_lesson": false,
    "sort_order": 3,
    "active": true,
    "teachers": [],
    "teacher_names": [],
    "title": "20-Class Package",
    "description": "20 x 60-minute private lessons. Best value. Valid for 6 months.",
    "lang": "en",
    "created_at": "2026-09-05T08:44:12.000000-05:00",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-05T08:44:12.000000-05:00"
  }

  ## Changelog
  - 2026-09-05: Added the `teachers` field -- an optional list of teacher UUIDs limiting who the package can be booked with. Empty (the default) keeps every package open to all active teachers, so existing packages are unaffected.
}
